From: Asuvath MS <asuvath.monikandan@adlinktech.com>
Subject: [PATCH] Modify UART4 peripherals domain permission to fix kernel abort

On LEC-iMX8MM the kernel enables uart4 (serial@30a60000). NXP's default RDC
configuration assigns UART4 to domain 1 (Cortex-M4), so the A53 register
access in imx_uart_probe() takes a synchronous external abort and panics
init. Grant UART4 to domain 0.

NOTE: ATF 2.14 carries two rdc[] tables, #ifdef IMX_ANDROID_BUILD and #else.
Both had UART4 as D1R|D1W, so the original hunk matched the Android table --
which Yocto never compiles. This targets the #else table that is actually built.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [board-specific]

Signed-off-by: Asuvath MS <asuvath.monikandan@adlinktech.com>
---
 plat/imx/imx8m/imx8mm/imx8mm_bl31_setup.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/plat/imx/imx8m/imx8mm/imx8mm_bl31_setup.c
+++ b/plat/imx/imx8m/imx8mm/imx8mm_bl31_setup.c
@@ -121,7 +121,7 @@
 	RDC_PDAPn(RDC_PDAP_UART1, D0R | D0W),
 	RDC_PDAPn(RDC_PDAP_UART2, D0R | D0W),
 	RDC_PDAPn(RDC_PDAP_UART3, D0R | D0W | D1R | D1W | D2R | D2W | D3R | D3W),
-	RDC_PDAPn(RDC_PDAP_UART4, D1R | D1W),
+	RDC_PDAPn(RDC_PDAP_UART4, D0R | D0W),
 
 	/* memory region */
 
